# Semantic Commit Messages

Always use Conventional Commits. Never use free-form subjects.

`type(scope): short imperative summary`

This applies to every git commit and every PR title. Squash-merge uses the PR title as the commit on `main`, which Release Please reads for `CHANGELOG.md` and `vX.Y.Z` tags.

## Allowed Types

Releasable (patch bump): `feat`, `fix`, `perf`, `deps`, `content`, `chore`, `revert`

Changelog-only: `docs`, `style`, `refactor`, `test`, `build`, `ci`

## Rules

- Always include a type. Prefer a scope (`content`, `seo`, `workflow`, `build`).
- Subject is concise, imperative, and has no ending punctuation.
- Use the body to explain why (1–2 sentences) when needed.
- If auto-PR fills a non-semantic title, fix the PR title before merge.

## Examples

```
✅ feat(content): publish two new blog posts for April 2026
✅ fix(seo): correct invalid frontmatter tags in blog posts
✅ chore(workflow): update auto-pr automation
❌ update stuff
❌ WIP
❌ chore/release-please-chore-types
```
